# An unknown head whose tail begins with a known method defines a named Structure and
# calls nothing, in every spelling (Q58; the author, 2026-10-05;
# docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#construction): `s: shout` and `t: shout()` retain the
# application of shout in their bodies without executing it, so shout prints nothing.
# report prints DONE (a C door keeps it native when the root is walked) and gives 7.
# The program says only DONE. Entry 7.
fn: shout () int
    c.printf: "called\n"
    return: 1

fn: report () int
    c.printf: "DONE\n"
    return: 7
end: report

s: shout
t: shout()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: report(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
